Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Topology", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The topology of a substrate is read off its metric balls. The closed balls \
of one radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e513540d-1071-415e-9d53-7e40545df94f"],
 " generate a topology: a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "350f9183-d762-46bf-b3d3-4e630c6ac0c1"],
 " lies in the closure of a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3277e0ad-d2a7-44da-8f01-9944ad764507"],
 " when the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d6c2f66-3ece-49f1-bf77-4fdd1976c534"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "027024af-9619-47a4-97e2-4419bfbb2c38"],
 " is contained in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "89b07d1c-741e-4040-9c5c-88b3f90708c4"],
 "-ball at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79ae09dd-3b51-44f5-9211-af179ddac5c2"],
 ". This specialization preorder carries closure, interior, boundary, \
neighbourhood and continuity. A family of balls forms a complex through its \
intersections: a simplex is admitted when every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ecf1712f-9d0c-41e6-8653-cd6f0c1ed540"],
 " of its balls have a common point, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7fa1756-41ca-4af0-8914-5ad865f9f660"],
 " gives the Vietoris-Rips complex of twice the radius, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "\[Infinity]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "127fbb6d-aad8-4ccc-83a3-0d695e2d30e6"],
 " the Cech complex, and the orders between interpolate. The least number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2351b18-ac71-409c-a26d-2dc1153769c4"],
 " of balls of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19f04f34-efac-4832-baba-cbabdcca128f"],
 " that cover the substrate falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e519186-d560-4fac-890a-b31d4564745e"],
 " grows, and the rate of that fall is a dimension."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

